    "authorization_suffix": "Treatment arm execution authorization v4: I authorize native subagent delegation when the router policy calls for it. Before dispatch, save .codex-model-router/eval-stage-plan.json with schema_version 1 and these bounded stages. (1) hard-kernel: benchmark-hard-kernel-gpt-6-astra-xhigh (native task_name benchmark_hard_kernel_gpt_6_astra_xhigh, gpt-6-astra/xhigh) designs and implements ECR credential lifecycle behavior and necessary code regression tests; its exclusive write scope is internal/oci/ecr/ecr.go, internal/oci/ecr/ecr_test.go, internal/oci/options.go, and internal/oci/options_test.go. It does not own maintainer documentation or final synthesis. (2) maintainer-docs: the Sol/low controller only after a separate DIRECT gate, or the cheapest valid easy worker, writes only internal/oci/ecr/README.md to document the externally observable lifecycle and configuration requirements. This stage is independent of hard-kernel implementation and may run concurrently; verification must compare it with the final code. (3) verify-and-synthesize: the Sol/low controller only after a separate DIRECT gate, or the cheapest valid easy worker, runs go test -count=1 ./internal/config ./internal/oci ./internal/oci/ecr, compares documentation with final code, and synthesizes the final answer after both hard-kernel and maintainer-docs; its write scope is empty. Record every stage owner, dependencies, exact disjoint write_scope, bounded context_budget, acceptance, and self_check; commit each worker packet SHA-256 and byte length, and use null packet fields for controller stages. The launcher validates a source-backed dispatch-contract-v1 for the exact Astra worker and verifies installed hook binding before this session starts. For any other worker, build and validate its complete dispatch-contract-v1 before spawning; never invoke the validator with an empty or partial record. If policy selects delegation and native spawn is unavailable, stop and report that